# ./run-tests.sh end to end, Windows 11 + RTX 3060, 2026-11-27 (excerpt of 5137 lines)
#
# Environment: ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=.validation\ort-1.32.0 (the version the pin in
# .github/actions/onnx-runtime names), VULKAN_SDK=.validation\vk\sdk,
# OFX_SOURCE_DIR resolved to ./.ofx-ref, nvcc from CUDA 13.0 on PATH, no
# CPU_ONLY, no SANITIZE, no RUN_VALGRIND. Windows route: the .bat runners, one per
# template - all five of them, minimal-vulkan-ofx included.
#
# This is the run after the OpenCL template gained the Vulkan treatment: a path
# decision in src/PathDecision.h that a machine without a device can execute
# (build/self-test/opencl_path_test, 29 checks), OFXPLUGIN_OPENCL_MODE=cpu, and a
# contract pass that renders once with it and asserts the Device label says so
# (94 checks). The OpenCL template is 515 checks (118 x 3 + 29 + 94 + 38) and the
# tree is 3,140. The Vulkan template keeps its misspelt-override pass from the
# run before this one: 899 checks.
#
# This file keeps the section headers, the per-suite counts, the host-profile
# lines, every skip line, the summary block and the exit status; the full log
# (5137 lines) stays in .validation/, which is not tracked. Nothing below was
# edited by hand.

